{
  "statement": "Safety and reliability are critical for the RollCall system to protect sensitive attendance data and ensure accurate reporting. SAF-01 ensures secure authentication to prevent unauthorized access, while SAF-02 guarantees real-time data synchronization for accurate attendance records. SAF-03 implements automated alerts for discrepancies, enhancing data accuracy. SAF-04 and SAF-05 focus on maintaining historical data and logging modifications for accountability. SAF-06 allows manual overrides during failures, and SAF-07 ensures regular security audits to identify vulnerabilities. These requirements collectively enhance the system's safety and reliability.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {"ids": ["GRN-01", "EFF-01"], "type": "resource", "description": "Real-time processing (EFF-01) may increase energy consumption, conflicting with GRN-01's focus on minimizing energy use, which could impact system reliability."},
    {"ids": ["TRU-01", "SAF-01"], "type": "logical", "description": "SAF-01's secure authentication may conflict with TRU-01's encryption if not properly integrated, potentially leading to vulnerabilities."},
    {"ids": ["EFF-05", "TRU-04"], "type": "resource", "description": "The requirement for students to view their records quickly (EFF-05) may conflict with the secure authentication process in TRU-04, potentially impacting performance."}
